# Emrakul is cast, not put onto the battlefield, so "When you cast this spell, take an extra turn after this one" triggers. Collector's
# Cage hides it (hideaway 5) and on turn 5 its counter makes three different powers: Bot1 plays Emrakul for free. Bot2 has
# two Islands and a Counterspell, and casts it on the Emrakul spell: it resolves anyway ("can't be countered"). The cast
# trigger resolves first (it is above the spell on the stack), so Bot1 also takes turn 6 (the extra turn), and Bot2 only
# gets turn 7.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Ornithopter
Plains
Llanowar Elves
Collector's Cage
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Emrakul, the Aeons Torn
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest x8

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Island
Counterspell
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Collector's Cage.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#1.Activate
Bot1.Arrange(Emrakul, the Aeons Torn | Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Collector's Cage.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Accept
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Stack.Emrakul, the Aeons Torn)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Emrakul, the Aeons Torn.Power = 15
? Bot2.Graveyard = Counterspell
[T6 Bot1.Main1]
? ActivePlayer = Bot1
[T7 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Turn = 7
ActivePlayer = Bot2
Bot1.Battlefield.Emrakul, the Aeons Torn.Power = 15
